INT. GRAND OPERA HOUSE - CATWALK ABOVE THE STAGE - NIGHT

Ropes, sandbags, pulleys in the dark. Below, a full orchestra tunes. A chandelier the size of a car hangs motionless beside the catwalk.

DETECTIVE INEZ CASTELLANO-WU, 40s, black blazer, radio clipped to her belt, creeps along the planks. Behind her: OFFICER BARNABAS FINCH, 20s, sweating through his uniform; STAGE MANAGER DOROTHEA LAMBERT, 50s, headset, whispering into her collar; and a pair of maintenance men, TOMASZ KRAWCZYK, 40s, and AUGUSTO ELEGBE, 30s, hauling a toolbox between them. At the far end of the catwalk, half in shadow, crouches a figure with a briefcase.

INEZ
(whispering)
Everybody quiet.

She raises a fist. They halt. Dorothea clamps a hand over her headset mic. Tomasz and Augusto set the toolbox down so slowly it makes no sound. Barnabas draws his sidearm and holds it at his chest.

DOROTHEA
(to Inez)
Overture starts in four minutes.

INEZ
Then we have four.

She steps forward. The planks creak. The figure at the end stiffens. A hush falls over the orchestra pit below.

FIGURE
(without turning)
I wouldn't come closer.

INEZ
Put the case down.

FIGURE
It's not a case. It's a promise.

Barnabas swallows. Augusto crosses himself. Tomasz mutters something in Polish.

TOMASZ
(muttering)
Boze, nie teraz.

DOROTHEA
(to the group)
Does anyone know where the cut-off is for the chandelier cable?

AUGUSTO
Stage left. Behind the fly rail.

DOROTHEA
Go. Quietly.

Augusto slips away. Inez keeps her eyes on the Figure.

INEZ
You don't have to do this.

FIGURE
Everyone says that.

INEZ
Because it's true.

The Figure turns. A woman, 50s, in evening dress and tennis shoes. VIOLETTA SANTORO-REYES, ex-soprano. Her face is wet. In her lap, the briefcase hums.

VIOLETTA
They fired me in this house. I sang four hundred nights.

INEZ
I know.

VIOLETTA
Do you? Do you know what silence sounds like when you were the music?

INEZ
No.

Violetta nods. Her fingers drift to the clasp. Barnabas lifts his gun.

OFFICER BARNABAS
Ma'am, stay still.

INEZ
(to Barnabas)
Lower it.

OFFICER BARNABAS
Detective --

INEZ
Lower it, Barnabas.

He lowers it. Violetta lets out a laugh, brittle and soft.

VIOLETTA
Four minutes, you said.

INEZ
Three.

VIOLETTA
Then let me sing it one last time.

DOROTHEA
(into the headset, low)
Hold the curtain. Hold it. Give me a spot on the catwalk.

A spotlight swings up from below and finds Violetta. She blinks. Rises. The briefcase slides from her lap. It clatters empty to the planks, a few pieces of sheet music spilling out.

Inez steps to it. Picks one up. It is an aria. Blank staves.

INEZ
(softly)
There's no bomb.

VIOLETTA
There never was.

Below, the orchestra falls silent. Waiting. Violetta takes a breath, lifts her chin, and sings one clear note into the dark. It carries up into the rafters. Nobody on the catwalk moves.

TOMASZ
(whispering, awed)
Matko Boska.

Dorothea lowers her hand. Barnabas holsters his gun. Inez closes her eyes.
